.TH RSV 1 "2026" "rsv-ng" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rsv \- runit service manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I command
[\fIservice\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsv
is a front-end for the
.BR sv (8)
and
.BR runsvdir (8)
utilities that makes managing runit services more convenient.
It handles both system-wide services (when run as root) and
per-user services (when run as a non-root user or with
.BR \-\-user ).
.PP
Most service commands accept one or more service names.
When multiple names are given, each is processed in turn;
a failure for one service is reported but does not prevent
the remaining services from being processed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-user
Operate on user services instead of system services.
Automatically set when the invoking user is not root.
.TP
\fB\-\-as\-user\fR \fIuser\fR
Manage another user's runit services.
Requires read/write access to that user's runit directories
(typically run as root).
.TP
.B \-\-now
Used with
.BR enable :
also start the service immediately after enabling it.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Used with
.BR new :
scaffold a
.BR svlogd (8)
log service alongside the main service.
.TP
.B \-\-errors
Used with
.BR logs :
show only lines matching \fIerror\fR, \fIwarn\fR, \fIcrit\fR, or \fIfail\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fIlevels\fR
Used with
.BR logs :
filter log output to lines matching the given comma-separated
level keywords (e.g.\& \fI\-\-level error,warn\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-lines\fR \fIN\fR
Used with
.BR logs :
show the last \fIN\fR matching lines before following new output
(default: 10).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-uptime
Used with
.BR list :
show the uptime of each running service.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIN\fR
Used with
.BR watch :
refresh every \fIN\fR seconds (default: 2).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Re-execute the command under
.BR bash (1)
.B \-x
tracing, then print a summary of functions called and key
path variables.
Useful for diagnosing unexpected behaviour.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Supervisor management
.TP
.B init
Start the user-mode
.BR runsvdir (8)
supervisor in the background.
Only valid in user mode.
Add \fBrsv \-\-user init\fR to your session startup file
(\fI~/.profile\fR, \fI~/.xinitrc\fR, etc.) to start it automatically.
.SS Service lifecycle
.TP
\fBstart\fR \fIservice\fR...
Start one or more services.
Each service must already be enabled.
.TP
\fBstop\fR \fIservice\fR...
Stop one or more running services.
.TP
\fBrestart\fR \fIservice\fR...
Restart one or more services.
Waits for each service to get a new PID before reporting success.
.TP
\fBreload\fR \fIservice\fR...
Send the reload signal (SIGHUP) to one or more services.
Not all services support reloading; an error is printed for those that do not.
.TP
\fBonce\fR \fIservice\fR...
Run one or more services once without supervision
(they will not be restarted if they exit).
.SS Enabling and disabling
.TP
\fBenable\fR [\fB\-\-now\fR] \fIservice\fR...
Create a symlink in
.I RUNSVDIR
so that
.BR runsvdir (8)
begins supervising the service.
With
.BR \-\-now ,
also start the service immediately.
.TP
\fBdisable\fR \fIservice\fR...
Stop and remove the supervision symlink for one or more services.
.SS Status and listing
.TP
\fBstatus\fR [\fIservice\fR...]
Without arguments, show the state of every enabled service.
With one or more service names, show detailed status for each,
including recent warnings and errors from the global log.
.TP
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-u\fR]
List all known services across all service directories, indicating
whether each is enabled/running, enabled/down, or disabled.
With
.BR \-u " / " \-\-uptime ,
also show the uptime of running services.
.TP
\fBwatch\fR [\fIservice\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIN\fR]
Display an auto-refreshing status view, similar to
.BR watch (1).
Without a service name, shows all enabled services.
.SS Logs
.TP
\fBlogs\fR [\fIservice\fR] [\fB\-\-errors\fR] [\fB\-\-level\fR \fIlevels\fR] [\fB\-\-lines\fR \fIN\fR]
Follow log output.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
With a service name: use the service's own
.BR svlogd (8)
log if one is configured, otherwise grep the global log.
.IP \(bu 2
Without a service name: follow the global log file.
.RE
.SS Service creation and editing
.TP
\fBnew\fR [\fB\-\-log\fR] \fIservice\fR
Scaffold a new service directory under
.IR SVDIR ,
creating a stub
.I run
script.
With
.BR \-\-log ,
also creates a
.BR svlogd (8)
log service.
Opens the run script for editing if confirmed.
.TP
\fBedit\fR \fIservice\fR...
Open the
.I run
script for one or more services in
.BR $EDITOR .
.SS Log service management
.TP
\fBlog\-setup\fR \fIservice\fR...
Add a
.BR svlogd (8)
log service to one or more existing services.
If the service is currently enabled, supervision is restarted
so that
.BR runsv (8)
picks up the new log directory.
.TP
\fBlog\-remove\fR \fIservice\fR...
Remove the
.BR svlogd (8)
log service from one or more services.
Log data on disk is left in place.
.SS Finish script
.TP
\fBfinish\-setup\fR \fIservice\fR...
Scaffold a
.I finish
script for one or more services.
The finish script is called by
.BR runsv (8)
whenever the service exits, and can be used to log the exit
code or suppress automatic restarts.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B doctor
Check for common runit configuration problems: dangling symlinks
in
.IR RUNSVDIR ,
missing or non-executable run scripts, services stuck in the
down state, and log services that are not being supervised.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage summary and exit.
.RB ( \-\-help
and
.B usage
are accepted as aliases.)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUNIT_SVDIR
Override the user-mode service definition directory
(default: \fI~/.runit/sv\fR).
.TP
.B RUNIT_RUNSVDIR
Override the user-mode active service directory
(default: \fI~/.runit/runsvdir\fR).
.TP
.B RUNIT_LOG
Override the path to the global log file used in user mode
(default: \fI~/.runit/log/everything/current\fR).
.TP
.B EDITOR ", " VISUAL
Editor opened by
.B edit
and
.BR new .
When running under
.BR sudo (8),
.B rsv
attempts to recover the real user's editor from their login
shell if these variables are stripped.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable all colour output (see \fIhttps://no-color.org\fR).
Colour is also disabled automatically when stdout is not a
terminal or
.B TERM
is set to
.IR dumb .
.TP
.B _RSV_DEBUG
Internal: enables
.B set \-x
tracing when the script re-invokes itself under
.BR \-\-debug .
Do not set this directly; use
.B \-\-debug
instead.
.SH FILES
.SS System paths (Void Linux)
.TP
.I /etc/sv
Service definition directory.
.TP
.I /var/service
Active service directory (RUNSVDIR).
.TP
.I /var/log/sv/everything/current
Global log file.
.SS System paths (Artix Linux)
.TP
.I /etc/runit/sv
Service definition directory.
.TP
.I /etc/runit/runsvdir/default
Active service directory (RUNSVDIR).
.TP
.I /var/log/everything/current
Global log file.
.SS System paths (Devuan)
.TP
.I /etc/sv ", " /usr/share/runit/sv.current
Service definition directories.
.TP
.I /etc/runit/runsvdir/default
Active service directory (RUNSVDIR).
.TP
.I /var/log/runit/everything/current
Global log file.
.SS User paths (all distros)
.TP
.I ~/.runit/sv
User service definition directory (override: \fB$RUNIT_SVDIR\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.runit/runsvdir
User active service directory (override: \fB$RUNIT_RUNSVDIR\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.runit/log/everything/current
User global log (override: \fB$RUNIT_LOG\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the user runsvdir supervisor at login:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv \-\-user init
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable and immediately start a system service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv enable \-\-now nginx
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable and start several services at once:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv enable \-\-now nginx redis postgresql
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch error-level log lines for a service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv logs \-\-errors nginx
.EE
.RE
.PP
Create a new user service with a log service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv \-\-user new \-\-log myapp
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check for configuration problems:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv doctor
.EE
.RE
.PP
Manage services belonging to another user (as root):
.PP
.RS
.EX
rsv \-\-as\-user alice status
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sv (8),
.BR runsvdir (8),
.BR runsv (8),
.BR svlogd (8),
.BR runit (8)
